/*
  AIQuietHoursSuggestion.strings
  TeslaSync — P4 shared surface · 0041 · AIQuietHoursSuggestion (Apple)

  The P1/S10 i18n catalog contribution for this surface. Every key the native surface resolves
  (table "AIQuietHoursSuggestion") lives here with its web `t(key, default)` English value. These
  entries fold into the app `Localizable.xcstrings` master catalog at integration time; they are
  kept in a per-surface table so each parallel surface prompt owns its own strings without editing
  the shared catalog.

  Group 1 is the EXACT set of keys from the web source (components/ai/AIQuietHoursSuggestion.tsx),
  including the two conditional preview notes (insufficient-history, existing-count). The web
  `{{start}}` / `{{end}}` / `{{tz}}` / `{{weekdays}}` / `{{severities}}` / `{{count}}` interpolation
  tokens are preserved verbatim and substituted at the display boundary by
  `QuietHoursSuggestionLogic.interpolate` (the native `t(key, vars)`). There is no web↔native key
  rename on this surface (no forbidden stub word appears in any key).

  Group 2 is the shared Helix scaffold keys the web `AIFeatureCard` / `AiOutputPanel` / `AIBadge`
  resolve (the universal "Ask Helix" CTA, the thinking label, the badge tooltip, the error label).

  Group 3 backs the native chrome — the VoiceOver proposal label, the friendly idle/empty hint, the
  P4 leaf freshness / loading / error copy — so the Swift sources hold no English literals.
*/

